{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH4A","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH4A","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.InstanceOnH4A","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.H4BasisBridge","lean:module:QOU.Shared.MarkovTraceClaim"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH4A.contextH4_has_far_commuting_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH4A.contextH4_has_far_commuting_pair","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceOnH4A.lean#L189-L195","doc":"The witness has a far-commuting pair of generator indices — the property\n`contextH3` cannot have, since `Generator 3` has only two indices and they are\nadjacent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH4A.contextH4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH4A.contextH4","kind":"def","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceOnH4A.lean#L172-L187","doc":"**A `MarkovTraceContext` at `n = 4`.**\n\n`contextH2`'s `cyclic` and `trace_prod_gen` are free; `contextH3`'s carry\ncontent but cannot reach a far-commuting pair. This one does both, on a carrier\nthat also carries `wedderburn₄` and `IsHeckeOfFullRank K 4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH4A.markovTraceH4A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH4A.markovTraceH4A","kind":"def","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceOnH4A.lean#L134-L170","doc":"**A Markov trace on `H₄(q)`**, for any Markov parameter `z`.\n\nEvery field carries content. `cyclic` is `QOU.Machinery.H4.trM4_cyclic` — a\ntheorem, not a consequence of commutativity, since `H₄(q)` is noncommutative —\nand `trace_prod_gen` must deliver all three ordered pairs, including the\nfar-commuting one.\n\nPreviously this was `H4Bridge.trM4_cyclic`, which transported the ASCII\n`trM_cyclic` across the basis relabelling and so depended on `gram_symm`'s 576\ncomputed entries. `H4.trM4_cyclic` proves the same statement directly from the\nthree generators, so that dependency — and the Gram chain behind it — is gone.\nNote the argument order differs: `(z, h, …)` here, against the bridge's\n`(h, z, …)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH4A.traceMap_s0_mul_s2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH4A.traceMap_s0_mul_s2","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceOnH4A.lean#L122-L130","doc":"**`tr(σ₀σ₂) = z²`** — the far-commuting pair, which does not exist below\n`n = 4`. Reaching its basis vector needs `farcomm02`: the word tree gives\n`σ₂σ₀ = b 8`, and the relation is what identifies that with `σ₀σ₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH4A.traceMap_s1_mul_s2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH4A.traceMap_s1_mul_s2","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceOnH4A.lean#L115-L120","doc":"`tr(σ₁σ₂) = z²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH4A.traceMap_s0_mul_s1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH4A.traceMap_s0_mul_s1","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceOnH4A.lean#L108-L113","doc":"`tr(σ₀σ₁) = z²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH4A.traceMap_s2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH4A.traceMap_s2","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceOnH4A.lean#L102-L104","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH4A.traceMap_s1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH4A.traceMap_s1","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceOnH4A.lean#L98-L100","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH4A.traceMap_s0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH4A.traceMap_s0","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceOnH4A.lean#L94-L96","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH4A.traceMap_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH4A.traceMap_one","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceOnH4A.lean#L88-L92","doc":"`tr(1) = 1`. The unit is basis vector `b 0` (`InstanceOnH4A.b_zero`), whose\nweight is `TRM4 … 0 = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH4A.traceMap_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH4A.traceMap_apply","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceOnH4A.lean#L85-L86","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH4A.traceMap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH4A.traceMap","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceOnH4A.lean#L79-L83","doc":"The Markov trace on `H₄(q)` at parameter `z`, as a `K`-linear functional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH4A.trM4_b","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH4A.trM4_b","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceOnH4A.lean#L73-L75","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH4A.trM4_e₄","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH4A.trM4_e₄","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceOnH4A.lean#L70-L71","signatureChunk":0}]}